{"step_index":1040,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T03:28:05Z","content":"Here is the color code reference used across the mission flowcharts and routing maps:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Mission Cards & Flow Elements\n\n| Color Swatch & Box | Category | Meaning & In-Game Function | Examples |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Warm Yellow / Cream**<br/>`#fef08a` fill<br/>`#ca8a04` border | **Mandatory Main Story Mission** | Core linear campaign missions required to advance the story. | • *1. Prologue*<br/>• *2. Gone Fishing*<br/>• *12. Buck Me*<br/>• *14. Clear Skies*<br/>• *19. Tourist Trap* |\n| **Peach / Warm Orange**<br/>`#ffedd5` fill<br/>`#ea580c` border | **Chapter Climax / Major Finale** | Narrative turning points, major heist executions, and chapter endings. | • *21. Discharge Time* (Ch. 1 Finale)<br/>• *44. Checking Out* (Ch. 2 Finale)<br/>• *70. The Cartel Heist* (Ch. 3 Finale)<br/>• *93. VCIA Takedown* (Ch. 4 Heist) |\n| **Light Purple / Lavender**<br/>`#f3e8ff` fill<br/>`#a855f7` border | **Any% Skippable Side Strand** | Optional side missions. In Chapter 1, these 7 missions are auto-completed by `func_10AA55` when Chapter 2 begins. | • *3. Unwanted Attention*<br/>• *4. Pipework*<br/>• *7. Lab Fees*<br/>• *8. Hey Arnold!*<br/>• *17. Don Gone*<br/>• *18. Recalibration* |\n| **Deep Green Badge**<br/>`#064e3b` fill<br/>`#10b981` border | **⚡ Speedrun Milestone & Skip** | Major mechanical milestones, time-saving routing notes, and chapter transition summaries. | • *Downtime Parallel Routing*<br/>• *Coffee Break (Dual Switching)*<br/>• *Ending B: The Deal (Fast Route)*<br/>• *Chapter 2 Transition* |\n| **Soft Pink / Rose**<br/>`#ffe4e6` fill<br/>`#f43f5e` border (♥) | **Relationship Tasks & Story Gates** | Optional romance/social activities (Hot Meter chores), or critical relationship/vehicle unlock gates. | • *6. Just a Scratch* (Mandatory Gate)<br/>• *Get Haircut / Flowers / Groceries*<br/>• *Lucia's Clothes* |\n| **White Diamond**<br/>`#ffffff` fill<br/>`#cbd5e1` border | **Decision & Gating Check** | Game logic forks evaluating whether prerequisites have been completed before opening next mission. | • *Did player finish Just a Scratch?*<br/>• *Are Day Release & Just a Scratch done?*<br/>• *Final Decision Standoff* |\n| **White Callout Pill**<br/>`#ffffff` fill<br/>`#71717a` border | **Communications & Triggers** | In-game events that trigger or follow missions: calls, texts, and cash pickups. | • `[CALL] Brian Call`<br/>• `[MSG] Joey Text`<br/>• `[MAILBOX] Donnie Text ($140)`<br/>• `[$] Deposit Cash into Buck Me` |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Arrow & Routing Connectors\n\n- **White Arrows (`#ffffff`)**: Standard chronological progression along the main storyline.\n- **Purple Arrows (`#a855f7`)**: Branching paths into optional/skippable side missions (e.g., from *Hey Arnold!* to *Island Dreams*, or from *Swamped* to *Don Gone*).\n- **Pink / Red Arrows (`#f43f5e`)**: Gating redirects (such as Joey intercepting progression and forcing you back to *Just a Scratch*) and inter-chapter transitions.\n- **Orange Arrows (`#ea580c`)**: Direct flow into high-stakes chapter finales (e.g., into *Discharge Time* or *The Cartel Heist*).\n- **Green Arrows (`#10b981`)**: The fastest Any% speedrun path (e.g., routing into *Ending B: The Deal* to bypass the Coast Guard boat chase).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Combined Master Map Column Borders\n\nOn 